# NOTICE

htokenmeter is an original implementation written for this project. It is not
a fork and contains no code from either project below; the design borrows
architectural patterns, which are ideas, not copyrightable expression.

Architecture references:

- one-api (https://github.com/songquanpeng/one-api), MIT License.
  Patterns referenced: the channel/ability/token data model, the
  pre-consume/settle relay flow, channel error classification for
  auto-disable, and the embedded web console approach.

- new-api (https://github.com/QuantumNous/new-api), AGPLv3.
  NO code was copied (its license would require this project to be AGPLv3).
  Patterns referenced only at the architectural level: multi-protocol
  downstream endpoints with auth header normalization, the multi-format
  adaptor interface, weighted channel selection, and billing safety
  invariants (centralized quota math, bounded billing multipliers).
